    "sourceDescription": "Figure 3. (A) Radiographs of a 13-year-old boy. The anteroposterior view of the left ankle joint shows the fracture line extending to the epiphysis. (B) Lateral view showing the fracture line extending from the posterior side of the tibial shaft to the anterior side of the epiphysis. The distal part of the epiphysis is displaced backward. This was classified as a Salter–Harris type II fracture. (C) At 6 months after the injury, the anteroposterior view of bilateral ankle joints shows no growth arrest lines. The epiphyseal plate of the affected side was blurred, while the epiphyseal plate of the contralateral side was still visible. This was judged as premature epiphyseal closure. (D) Lateral view of bilateral ankle joints showing also premature closure of the epiphyseal plate of the affected side.",
